  "notes": "Compound of {初心|しょしん} (beginner's mind) + {者|しゃ} (person). Used for any skill, hobby, or activity.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {初心者|しょしんしゃ}{向|む}け: for beginners, beginner-friendly\n- {初心者|しょしんしゃ}{用|よう}: for beginners (use)\n- {初心者|しょしんしゃ}コース: beginner course\n- {初心者|しょしんしゃ}マーク: beginner driver mark (green and yellow {若葉|わかば} symbol)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nNew drivers in Japan must display the {初心者|しょしんしゃ}マーク for one year after getting their license.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ビギナー: beginner (loanword, casual)\n- {素人|しろうと}: amateur, layperson (can be slightly dismissive)\n- {未経験者|みけいけんしゃ}: person without experience (formal, often in job listings)",
